<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell Cochin high aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell Cochin high aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting January 20-25 from Cochin on the west coast, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes January 9, and is valid until January 10.</p>
<p>In its last HAN tender from the west coast, IOC sold 25,000 tonnes for December 22-24 lifting at $16.65 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, free-on-board Cochin.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3086)</p>
